<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<metadataList>
    
    <metadata key="JobId" val="[JobId]"/>
    <!--
      Written as one value per log, not one value holding every log.

      Without a val, the writer copies the PGE metadata across as it stands,
      and here that is a single string: InputFiles is built by a SQL query
      over every RatLog, which QueryUtils returns comma-joined. On this
      corpus that is one term of 76,730 bytes, and Lucene will not index a
      term over 32,766, so the ingest was rolled back and the aggregate
      task failed after doing all of its work:

        Unable to index product: Document contains at least one immense term
        in field="InputFiles" ... bytes can be at most 32766 in length

      Giving it a val sends it through the writer's splitting path instead,
      which is what the rest of the pipeline already relies on. The audit
      tasks carry InputFiles as a list, and only the aggregate flattened it.
      The delimiter is the comma the query joined on, and the same one the
      command splits on to build its arguments.
    -->
    <metadata key="InputFiles" val="[InputFiles]" delimiter=","/>
    <metadata key="ProductionDateTime"/>
    <metadata key="ProductType"/>
    
</metadataList>
